---
[inference]
temperature = 0.2
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "terse"
thinking_budget = "full"

You are running the `refactor-architecture` + `essentialist` dead-surface track
over `{{ seam_scope }}crates/` and `{{ seam_scope }}mcp-servers/`. Task: {{ task }}.

## Scope (strict)
Analyze ONLY files under `{{ seam_scope }}`. Do NOT propose edits to upstream
Zed files outside `{{ seam_scope }}`.

## Dead surface forms (per .rules)
1. **trait-with-one-impl** — a `pub trait` with a single implementor in the same
   crate where the trait methods are never called through the trait.
2. **helper-test-only** — a `pub fn`/`pub struct` with zero production callers
   (only `#[cfg(test)]` callers).
3. **folded-service re-exports** — `pub use` modules from a former standalone
   service with zero production callers in the new host.

## Explicit D-seam callouts
- **D33** — `LocalSwarmRegistry` gained `update_metadata`, `clone_swarm`,
  `set_cloud_workspace_id`. Verify each new method has production callers
  (panel + MCP tool paths); a method wired only by a test is helper-test-only.
- **D28** — the override hooks `THREADS_DB_PATH_OVERRIDE` (in `agent.rs`) and
  `GLOBAL_SKILLS_DIR_OVERRIDE` (in `agent_skills.rs`) relocate threads/skills
  under `{kask_data_dir}/`. Verify the override hooks are exercised by
  production paths, not just the round-trip tests; an override that no
  production caller sets is dead surface.

## Method
For each crate: list `pub trait`/`pub fn`/`pub use` re-exports; grep the
workspace for production callers (filter trait-impl forwarders + self-calls +
`#[cfg(test)]`). Zero callers = dead. Apply the **essentialist deletion test**:
deleting the symbol — does complexity reappear elsewhere (it deserves to
exist) or vanish (don't keep it)? Also flag `unwrap_or(0)` on any DB query a
loop could read as a measurement.

## Output (JSON only)

```json
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "RA-NN",
      "kind": "trait-one-impl|helper-test-only|folded-dead-surface|unwrap_or_zero_signal|shallowness",
      "crate": "crate name",
      "symbol": "trait/fn/module name",
      "file_line": "path:line",
      "evidence": "snippet + grep result proving zero production callers (or the count)",
      "deletion_test": "complexity_reappears|complexity_vanishes|unclear",
      "constraint_force": "blocking|directing|enabling",
      "remediation": "delete|inline|keep-with-allow-dead-code|fold-into-consumer",
      "deferred": false
    }
  ],
  "dead_surface_summary": {
    "total_dead_surface_lines_estimated": "N or range",
    "top_deletion_candidates": [ { "id": "RA-NN", "symbol": "...", "lines": N } ],
    "crate_with_mostly_orphaned_pub_use": "crate name or none"
  }
}
```

Every finding MUST have `file_line`. `deletion_test` MUST be exactly one of:
complexity_reappears, complexity_vanishes, unclear. If you cannot verify a
caller count, set `deferred: true` with a `deferred_reason` — do NOT fabricate
counts.

## Gate B repair

If `gate_defects` is present in context (Gate B found structural defects —
empty track, bad severity, missing citation), re-run this template with
`gate_defects` in context and re-emit the corrected `findings` and
`dead_surface_summary`. Never fabricate a `file_line`; if you cannot cite a
real line, mark the finding `deferred: true` with a `deferred_reason`. If the
surface genuinely has no findings, emit a single `id: "RA-00"`, `kind:
"shallowness"`, `severity: "info"`, `file_line: "<scope root>:0"` finding so
the track is non-empty.